    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="d121-2" n="2" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76ve10/pgd121-2"/>

                <head>122. Telegram 149761 From the Department of State to the Embassy in
                        Brazil<anchor n="1" xml:id="d122-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d122-f2"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1969-09-04T22:56:00+00:00">September 4, 1969, 2256Z</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <pb facs="d122-1" n="1" xml:id="pgd122-1"/>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>Reference:</head>
                    <item>Belton/Dean Telcon</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subject:</label>
                    <item>Kidnapping of Ambassador</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. Concerning demands contained in kidnapper’s note, our position vis-a-vis
                        GOB should be that safe return of Amb Elbrick
                    is of over-riding importance to us and we urge that all measures be taken,
                    including compliance with kidnapper’s demands if necessary. Should it appear
                    that any GOB strategy concerning the search is carrying them dangerously close
                    to the 48-hour deadline without locating the Ambassador, you should reiterate
                    forcefully our desire for GOB compliance with kidnappers’ demands.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d122-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d122-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1967–69, POL 23–9 BRAZ. Secret; Exdis; Flash. Drafted by Dean; cleared by
                        Meyer and Executive Secretary
                        Eliot; and approved by Richardson.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d122-f2" n="2" xml:id="d122-f2-content">
                <p>Under Secretary Richardson stated that the U.S. Government should comply with the
                    demands of the kidnappers to secure Ambassador Elbrick’s release.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
